Falsifies `non_volatile_memory_express::verification::a_transfer_command_is_only_built_for_a_block_the_namespace_has`.

The defect: `Namespace::holds_whole_block` drops its `checked_add(1)`, so it bounds the block's first byte rather than
its last. The block one past the end of the namespace is then accepted and a command is built
for an LBA the namespace does not have.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!((block + 1) * 4096 <= namespace.capacity_bytes)`. The harness's own `(block + 1) *
4096` also overflows for a huge `block` under this patch, so Kani reports that check too; both
are the same escape seen from the harness's side.

diff --git a/crates/non_volatile_memory_express/src/namespace.rs b/crates/non_volatile_memory_express/src/namespace.rs
index 808babc19..e036d665b 100644
--- a/crates/non_volatile_memory_express/src/namespace.rs
+++ b/crates/non_volatile_memory_express/src/namespace.rs
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@ impl Namespace {
     /// Name: ratified 2026-11-03 (#3118). The check is that the entire block fits (`end <= capacity`),
     /// not only that its start lies inside, hence `holds_whole_block`.
     pub fn holds_whole_block(&self, block: u64, unit: u64) -> bool {
-        match block.checked_add(1).and_then(|n| n.checked_mul(unit)) {
+        match Some(block).and_then(|n| n.checked_mul(unit)) {
             Some(end) => end <= self.capacity_bytes,
             None => false,
         }
